# OpenSSL advisories in the FROZEN runtime base image
# gcr.io/distroless/nodejs20-debian12. Google stopped rebuilding the
# nodejs20 distroless line after Node 20 reached end of life, so its
# libssl3 (3.0.18) never receives the Debian security patches; every
# build of any app fails the HIGH,CRITICAL image gate on these seven
# CVEs. Exposure is theoretical for our services: Node bundles its own
# statically linked OpenSSL and nothing dlopen()s the distroless
# libssl3, but the scanner flags installed packages, not usage.
#
# TEMPORARY: delete this file when the runtime moves to a maintained
# distroless line (nodejs22/nodejs24) — the Node 24 + Express 5
# migration branch owns that change.
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
CVE-2026-28390
CVE-2026-45447
CVE-2026-84782
